Yet Another Dangerous Bones Death 
(Note: that does not exclude stupidity as cause of death)

I just uploaded a dangerous bones file via hearse.
Normally I wouldn't comment on that, but I'll do it 
nevertheless because I myself fell victim to those bones 
(so it's a double bones now).

I was playing illiterate and vegetarian. Originally it
had also been atheist but I gave up on that when I had
to decide between atheist and illiterate. Still I kept
to half of it, meaning not donating and not dropping 
things on altars, sacrificing, or praying for any purpose
other than strict surviving.

I was going ok., my AC was down to -2 but my two dogs
had been turned into orc zombie and gremlin by the same
polytrap (I never use polytraps intentionally) that was
one level above the bigroom. The gremlin was killed 
shortly after, but I took the orc zombie down into the
Bigroom where I left it behind when I made a hasty 
retreat after realizing what was going on down there.

At first the level looked normal enough. There were quite
a lot of monsters to the left, and only a few to the right.
The upstairs were nearer to the left than to the right side
and the space around the upstairs and between the two 
staircases was free. The first thing I noticed that was 
alarming was a purple 'h'. Check: a dwarf king ... whew!
Next to it, there was a purple 'H' which turned out to be
a titan called Doggy - so it was a bones file. This made me
scour the level more carefully and sure enough, there also
was a purple 'L' called Kitty. I didn't have any method to
protect myself against touch of death, so I fled back up,
and thought about my options. I killed some time in the Mines
which was quite dangerous seeing that I still didn't have any
intrinsic apart from sleep resistance (elven Ranger), 
although I ate all the molds I could find, and also a couple 
of blue jellies. Well, I survived the Mines but didn't find 
any helpful wand or weapon (my best weapons were my +1 Sting 
and my +1 elven bow, dagger Expert, bow skilled). There were 
two magic lamps in Minetown both of which I bought. I possessed 
one clear potion that I had named 'non-cursed' because my dogs
had stepped on it. I dipped one of the lamps into the potion 
and it glowed amber. Unluckily, when I rubbed the lamp out came
a hostile djinni ("You disturbed me, fool!") who fell quickly
to a couple of +2 elven arrows. The second lamp couldn't be 
blessed but I tried it nevertheless but this time the djinni
only was peaceful. Darn! I had so hoped on GDSM.
Then I remembered the black dragon scales that I had acquired
from a dragon that was created by the polytrap, and that I had 
managed to kill it using /sleep and my trusty Sting.
Now my plan was to polymorph into a black dragon and blast the 
lich and titan into oblivion. Part of it worked...

When I went in the titan was on a line with me, so I used 
#monster at once but missed. Next move the master lich moved in
and touched me with a freeze attack. Twice did I blast it and
missed both times, but in the third try it worked. Only the turn
before the lich had called in some of his friends, among them 
a mind flayer and a disenchanter. Now, as soon as I had killed 
Kitty (the lich) the flayer started sucking my brain out which
was made easy by the fact that in my dragon form naturally I 
wasn't wearing any helmet. I was down to very few HP, something
hit me, I turned human again (with the scales as only armor).
Then someone threw a potion at me, and then everyone was hitting 
me. 
... killed by a disenchanter. Place 30 of 100, not bad after all.

Anyway, as I said the game left bones, but IMHO the most 
dangerous opponent was disposed of. The mean thing about it is
that all monsters are gathered around the upstairs.

So have fun, all ye hearse users! ;-]

